title: March 2026

@p2050_name_2026
# prose-audit: Grade B — Hołownia and the incoming chair now carry the rebrand as an institutional test, and all four Lewica responses have distinct aftermaths; the scene remains a small identity bulletin rather than a full leadership contest.
title: Poland 2050 removes Hołownia's name
subtitle: The registry can remove a founder's name more easily than a movement can replace his electorate
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-holownia.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 22
order: 20
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2026 and month = 3 and p2050_leader != "Szymon Hołownia"
on-arrival: p2050_ideology = "Centrist institutionalism · post-founder survival"; news_headline = "Poland 2050 RP begins life after its founder's name"

= March 2026 — A party after the personality

When <span class="party-p2050"><b>Szymon Hołownia</b></span> founded the movement, even the registered name said
that Poland 2050 was his project. Chair **[+ p2050_leader +]** now asks the
delegates to remove that possessive and continue as **Poland 2050 RP**: an
organisation meant to outlive its television founder, presidential campaigns
and first parliamentary generation.

[? if third_way_active: The renamed party remains one half of Third Way. PSL
president <span class="party-psl"><b>Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz</b></span> welcomes continuity and immediately
asks whether the new independence will extend to joint candidate lists.?][? if
third_way_split: Without PSL's joint list, the new signboard also exposes
Poland 2050 to the electoral threshold on its own.?]

Lewica can recognise an institutional transition, use the moment to reopen
list talks, reinforce the surviving centrist pact or invite the party into a
larger social-development project. None of those choices gives us ownership of
the name or its members.

- @name_respect
- @name_lists
- @name_third_way
- @name_left_union

@name_respect
title: Treat the rebrand as a legitimate institutional transition
subtitle: Recognise the new chair's authority without turning courtesy into an electoral promise.
on-arrival: p2050_relation += 3; public_trust += 1; government_coalition_dissent -= 1; news_headline = "The Left recognises a centrist party rather than a former celebrity movement"

Lewica addresses its congratulations to **Chair [+ p2050_leader +]** and Poland
2050's elected bodies, not to Hołownia's former personal office. The gesture
costs us no list place and promises no coalition. It does make later talks less
likely to begin with a demand that we prove the party itself is real.

- @poland_event_queue: Send the congratulations

@name_lists
title: Open 2027 common-list talks while the brand is weak
subtitle: Offer threshold shelter now, before the renamed party learns whether voters will follow it alone.
view-if: third_way_split = 1
on-arrival: p2050_relation += 2; ko_relation -= 2; local_network += 2; public_trust -= 1; news_headline = "Threshold arithmetic enters the coalition two years early"

Regional negotiators compare constituencies while the paint on Poland 2050's
new offices is still fresh. **[+ p2050_leader +]** accepts talks but refuses to
describe them as rescue. KO reads the same meeting as Lewica bidding for the
centre with protected list places rather than a common programme.

- @poland_event_queue: Open the constituency talks

@name_third_way
title: Publish the surviving Third Way's 2027 list rules
subtitle: Make the post-founder party bind itself publicly to PSL before another leadership crisis reopens the pact.
view-if: third_way_active = 1
on-arrival: third_way_future = "Named 2027 Third Way candidates and list rules"; third_way_cohesion += 5; psl_relation += 3; p2050_relation += 2; local_network += 1; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "The post-founder party binds itself to Third Way's next joint list"

**[+ p2050_leader +]** and Kosiniak-Kamysz publish nomination rules, campaign
accounts and a procedure for settling constituency disputes. Lewica signs only
as a parliamentary witness. Third Way remains their pact, but neither partner
can now abandon it while claiming that no terms ever existed.

- @poland_event_queue: Witness the published rules

@name_left_union
title: Invite Poland 2050 into a broader social-development party
subtitle: Offer a congress rather than list shelter, but only from a position strong enough to make the invitation credible.
choose-if: left_poll >= 14 and party_system_left_pull >= 18 and p2050_relation >= 40
unavailable-subtitle: Poland 2050 still sees more safety in centrist autonomy.
on-arrival: left_realign_invite_p2050 = 1; p2050_relation += 6; ko_relation -= 4; party_unity += 1; news_headline = "Lewica invites Poland 2050 to negotiate a common social-development party"

Lewica sends a written invitation to **[+ p2050_leader +]**: not annexation and
not a one-election cartel, but a congress on public investment, services and
institutional reform. Poland 2050 agrees to send delegates without dissolving
itself. KO condemns the initiative as an attempt to replace the democratic
centre; our own organisers welcome finally negotiating from strength.

- @poland_event_queue: Send the invitation
